# Domain model (crates/domain)

Pure: no IO, no clock, no Claude knowledge. Time arrives inside events (`Timestamp`, ms).

## Aggregate

`WarRoom` (room.rs) holds `Session`s by id and is the only entry point: `apply(SessionEvent) ->
Option<AttentionChange>`. A session is created by the first event that carries a `SessionContext`;
intents about unknown sessions are ignored (and therefore not persisted).

## Status → attention (session.rs)

| Status | Attention | Set by |
|---|---|---|
| `AwaitingYou { reason, tool, detail }` | `NeedsYou` | permission request, question tools, elicitation |
| `AwaitingInput` + `unseen` | `Finished` | `TurnEnded` (Stop); `IdlePrompt` only if a turn end was missed |
| `Working { tool }`, `Compacting` | `Working` | prompt, tools, compaction (a `Started` after compaction resumes Working) |
| `Idle`, `AwaitingInput` seen | `Idle` | start, `Seen`, `Interrupted` (you stopped the turn: no notice) |
| `Ended { reason }` | `Offline` | SessionEnd, or `ProcessLost` from the liveness tick |

`Attention` is ordered by urgency; the tray color is the max over sessions **on watch** (not archived,
not muted). `deserves_notice()` = on watch + alerting + actually changed.

## Rules that are easy to break

- A second `AwaitingYou` for the same wait (the Notification after a PermissionRequest) must not wipe
  the tool/detail already known.
- `PromptSubmitted` un-archives: writing to a dismissed session brings it back. That is the product
  definition of "archive" (dismiss without killing).
- Subagent tool events (`SubagentTool`) never change the main session's tool — but they resolve a
  pending permission (the agent moved on).
- Finished subagents are kept (last 6) so their work can be inspected; `Ended` finishes the running ones.
- "Stuck" is **not** a domain state: it is derived from `last_activity_at` and the clock in
  `crates/application/src/view.rs::stalled_since` (see `architecture.mdc`).

## Persistence compatibility (hard rule)

`SessionEvent`s are stored as JSON forever (14-day retention, 3-day replay). New fields need
`#[serde(default)]`; never rename or remove serde tags/fields; add variants, don't reshape old ones.
`room.rs` has a test that loads an event from before newer fields existed — extend it when you add one.
